   **Goal:**  
   The workflow will take the experimental crystal structure of the protein–ATP complex, clean it by removing crystallographic Mg²⁺ ions and any water molecules, add missing hydrogens, and validate the integrity of the remaining components. It will then generate a fully parameterised GROMACS system using the AMBER99SB‑ILDN force field for the protein and GAFF2 for ATP, solvate the complex in a cubic TIP3P box with a 1.2 nm buffer, add 0.15 M NaCl, and produce two independent 200 ns production‑run MDP files with distinct random seeds. The final deliverables will be a cleaned PDB file, a GROMACS topology, a solvated coordinate file, and two production MDP files ready for equilibration and production.
   
